{{- define "cli-failure-recovery" -}}

=== CLI FAILURE RECOVERY ===
After repeated CLI failure, stop retrying and preserve the exact failing command and observed error.
Structured safe_action takes precedence. Use this fallback only when no lifecycle result is available and a fresh task query confirms your authority and the recovery operation's preconditions; otherwise stop or requery without a mutation.
Fenced state-lock acquisition retries until success or cancellation, keeping the original request-id and expected-transition.

{{if eq .RoleType "doer"}}For a state-lock timeout hold, add --state-lock-timeout to mark-blocked only if no human ask, repair, rejection RCA, preparation or unmet dependency remains.
EXECUTABLE RECOVERY COMMAND:
`{{binaryName}} mark-blocked {{.TaskID}} --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --reason "Repeated CLI failure. Exact command: <exact failing command>. Observed error: <observed error>." --questions "Which prerequisite or external state must change?" --json`
{{else if eq .RoleType "reviewer"}}EXECUTABLE RECOVERY COMMAND:
`{{binaryName}} submit-verdict {{.TaskID}} REJECTED --review-commit {{.ReviewCommit}} --reason "Repeated CLI failure. Exact command: <exact failing command>. Observed error: <observed error>." --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json`

NON-EXECUTABLE REFERENCE:
`{{binaryName}} mark-blocked` is doer-only and MUST NOT be executed by reviewers.
{{end}}
{{- end -}}
